From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] aic_load_fw: a timed-out firmware message fails and is freed

From code reading (pinned tag plus the series; kernel 6.18.53).

cmd_mgr_queue() waits for a blocking message's confirmation with
wait_for_completion_killable_timeout(). Two exits of that wait are wrong:

- Timeout (0): it stores -ETIMEDOUT in cmd->result, calls cmd_complete(),
  which sets cmd->result back to 0 for a waiting command, and returns 0.
  rwnx_send_msg() passes that 0 on, so the caller counts the message as
  confirmed and reads a cfm buffer the firmware never filled. The command
  is taken off the list but never freed.
- Killed (< 0, -ERESTARTSYS): it is treated like a confirmation and the
  command is freed while it is still on cmd_mgr->cmds. A confirmation
  arriving afterwards walks cmd_mgr_msgind() into freed memory, and its
  memcpy() can land in a caller's stack buffer after that caller has
  returned.

The timeout also marks the command manager crashed, so the next message
fails with -EPIPE; only a timeout on the last message of a sequence
went unseen.

In the vendor driver: it reuses cmd_complete(), the confirmation's
completion path, as the timeout's cleanup, and cmd_complete() reports
success by design; and it reads a non-zero wait result as "completed".

What changes: on timeout or kill, and only if no confirmation completed
the command in the meantime (RWNX_CMD_FLAG_DONE, read under
cmd_mgr->lock, which cmd_mgr_msgind() holds while it touches a command),
the command is taken off the list under the lock. A timeout returns
-ETIMEDOUT and still marks the manager crashed; a kill returns the wait's
error. The command is freed on every exit of a blocking message.

Not taken:
- Keeping cmd_complete() and returning cmd->result afterwards:
  cmd_complete() would have to learn to tell a timeout from a
  confirmation, and it also runs from the rx path.
- Clearing the crashed state after a timeout: the vendor's reason (a
  firmware that stopped answering) stands; the probe fails anyway.

Test stimulus and counter under /sys/module/aic_load_fw/parameters:
rx_loader_inject_cmd_timeout (0644): cmd_mgr_msgind() drops the next N
confirmations that match a waiting command, so that command runs into its
real timeout (RWNX_80211_CMD_TIMEOUT_MS, 2 s per queued command). A zero
wait does not work as a stimulus: aicwf_usb_bus_txmsg() waits for its own
URB, and the confirmation has arrived by the time cmd_mgr_queue() waits.
rx_loader_cmd_timeouts (0444) counts timed-out messages.

Falsifier, on the board, with the part at its loaded id
(inject a command timeout):
  modprobe -r aic8800_fdrv aic_load_fw
  modprobe aic_load_fw
  echo 1 > /sys/module/aic_load_fw/parameters/rx_loader_inject_cmd_timeout
The first probe reboots the part and returns before modprobe does; the
parameter is armed before the part comes back at its boot id. The first
message of the second probe's system_config_8800d80() is the read of
0x40500000. Without the fix it returns 0, and the configuration goes on
until the next message fails on the crashed manager with -32 (-EPIPE).
With it: "40500000 rd fail: -110", and rx_loader_cmd_timeouts 1. A -32
with the fix refutes it.

Assisted-by: Claude


diff --git a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic_load_fw/aicbluetooth_cmds.c b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic_load_fw/aicbluetooth_cmds.c
index 223cfc8..539fe03 100644
--- a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic_load_fw/aicbluetooth_cmds.c
+++ b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic_load_fw/aicbluetooth_cmds.c
@@ -44,6 +44,16 @@ static void cmd_complete(struct rwnx_cmd_mgr *cmd_mgr, struct rwnx_cmd *cmd)
     }
 }
 
+/* Test stimulus: the next N confirmations that match a waiting command
+ * are dropped, so that command runs into its real timeout.
+ */
+static int rx_loader_inject_cmd_timeout;
+module_param(rx_loader_inject_cmd_timeout, int, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(rx_loader_inject_cmd_timeout, "Test stimulus: drop the next N confirmations of waiting firmware messages, so they time out");
+static uint rx_loader_cmd_timeouts;
+module_param(rx_loader_cmd_timeouts, uint, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(rx_loader_cmd_timeouts, "Blocking firmware messages that timed out and were taken off the command list");
+
 static int cmd_mgr_queue(struct rwnx_cmd_mgr *cmd_mgr, struct rwnx_cmd *cmd)
 {
     bool defer_push = false;
@@ -98,21 +108,37 @@ static int cmd_mgr_queue(struct rwnx_cmd_mgr *cmd_mgr, struct rwnx_cmd *cmd)
 
     if (!(cmd->flags & RWNX_CMD_FLAG_NONBLOCK)) {
         unsigned long tout = msecs_to_jiffies(RWNX_80211_CMD_TIMEOUT_MS * cmd_mgr->queue_sz);
-        if (!wait_for_completion_killable_timeout(&cmd->complete, tout)) {
-            printk(KERN_CRIT"cmd timed-out\n");
-
-            cmd_dump(cmd);
+        long left = wait_for_completion_killable_timeout(&cmd->complete, tout);
+        int ret = 0;
+
+        if (left <= 0) {
+            /* Timed out (0) or killed (< 0). The command may still be on
+             * the list, where cmd_mgr_msgind() finds it under the lock;
+             * take it off before freeing it, and report the failure: the
+             * caller would otherwise go on with a cfm buffer the
+             * firmware never filled.
+             */
             spin_lock_bh(&cmd_mgr->lock);
-            cmd_mgr->state = RWNX_CMD_MGR_STATE_CRASHED;
             if (!(cmd->flags & RWNX_CMD_FLAG_DONE)) {
-                cmd->result = -ETIMEDOUT;
-                cmd_complete(cmd_mgr, cmd);
+                list_del(&cmd->list);
+                cmd_mgr->queue_sz--;
+                if (left == 0) {
+                    printk(KERN_CRIT"cmd timed-out\n");
+                    cmd_dump(cmd);
+                    cmd_mgr->state = RWNX_CMD_MGR_STATE_CRASHED;
+                    rx_loader_cmd_timeouts++;
+                    ret = -ETIMEDOUT;
+                } else {
+                    ret = left;
+                }
             }
+            /* else the confirmation completed it just after the wait
+             * ended: it is off the list and the cfm buffer is filled.
+             */
             spin_unlock_bh(&cmd_mgr->lock);
         }
-        else{
-            kfree(cmd);
-        }
+        kfree(cmd);
+        return ret;
     } else {
         cmd->result = 0;
     }
@@ -147,6 +173,12 @@ static int cmd_mgr_msgind(struct rwnx_cmd_mgr *cmd_mgr, struct rwnx_cmd_e2amsg *
         if (cmd->reqid == msg->id &&
             (cmd->flags & RWNX_CMD_FLAG_WAIT_CFM)) {
 
+            if (unlikely(rx_loader_inject_cmd_timeout > 0)) {
+                rx_loader_inject_cmd_timeout--;
+                found = true;
+                break;
+            }
+
             if (!cmd_mgr_run_callback(cmd_mgr, cmd, msg, cb)) {
                 found = true;
                 cmd->flags &= ~RWNX_CMD_FLAG_WAIT_CFM;
